    ],
    "notes": "Sheet shows MAIN PANEL schematic with two multi-core cables (MU5-12, MU4-12, MU4a-12/1) connecting left-side terminal strips (T/S E, T/S F) to PLUG A/B/C terminal blocks feeding a central dotted-outline PC CARD / ALARM MODULE enclosure. This enclosure contains multiple diode arrays (small diode symbols in rows) feeding output taps labelled with load names (ANCHOR LIGHT, MAST UP LIGHTS, FWD/STERN NAV LIGHTS, STEAMING LT, SPREADER/FORE DECK/RED/GREEN LTs, various BILGE/SUMP pumps, GREY/BLACKWATER pump run indicators and alarms). To the right, a column of manual switches/selectors (S8-S19) drives lamp and pump outputs; some (S16,S17) have ON/OFF/AUTO positions for pump control, S18/S19 for blackwater pumps. Bottom of PC card enclosure holds a small relay/buzzer/horn assembly with MUTE(S15)/TEST(S14) pushbuttons feeding an external buzzer/horn icon at far right. Lower section of sheet has additional terminal blocks (T/S C, T/S E) and Plug B/C blocks routing to Emergency Stop (S1), Emergency Lts (S12), Courtesy Lts outputs, and an ALARM MOD 2 PORT PEDESTAL block with its own Plug C interconnect and mute switch. Several wire-gauge/junction diamond callouts appear on cable runs (not enumerated individually here per instructions). Some terminal numbers on far upper-left column (7,8,9,10,12,15,19-24) are small and partly compressed; legibility fair. Cross-reference pointers to DWG 120 and DWG 114 are explicit drawing continuations and are recorded as such.",
    "_model": "claude-sonnet-5",
